+/*
+ * vf_dlssnr.c -- DLSS 5 NR (NGX feature 18) as an in-chain mpv filter.
+ *
+ * The model itself is not in this process. NVIDIA's nvngx_dlssnr.dll is a
+ * Windows binary, so it runs inside a Wine helper (dlssnr-helper) that reads a
+ * request from shared memory and writes an answer back. This filter is the
+ * client: it owns everything around the round trip.
+ *
+ * ── Why in the chain and not at present time ──────────────────────────────
+ * NeuralScreen's Vulkan layer runs at vkQueuePresentKHR -- after the frame was
+ * composed. Frame generation (vf_vfg) sits earlier in mpv's chain, so a
+ * present-stage NR would denoise frames that had already been generated, and
+ * the generated ones would have been interpolated from un-denoised sources.
+ * As a filter, NR runs on real decoded frames and VFG then synthesises from
+ * clean ones. Order in the chain is therefore load-bearing:
+ *
+ *     hwdec → [hwup] → [vsr/truehdr] → dlssnr → vfg → VO
+ *
+ * ── Geometry ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
+ * Everything is done at or below panel resolution. For a 2160p source on a
+ * 1440p panel the source is resampled to 1440p once, on the GPU, and every
+ * later stage (model proxy, delta, composite, VFG) works on 1440p. NR is not
+ * an upscaler here: `size=panel` only ever shrinks.
+ *
+ * Inside that target the model can be handed a smaller raster (work_scale).
+ * At 0.5 a 1440p target gives the model a 720p proxy; the answer comes back
+ * at 720p, its *delta* is upscaled to 1440p and composited onto the 1440p
+ * anchor. This is NeuralScreen's "working scale" with the same meaning --
+ * the helper has no idea it exists, it only ever sees the raster it is given.
+ * Measured on this machine (2 passes, cinematic): 720p ≈ 10 ms, 960p ≈ 20 ms,
+ * 1080p ≈ 16 ms, 1440p ≈ 25 ms per frame.
+ *
+ * ── Colour ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
+ * The model only accepts an 8-bit SDR proxy; it refuses to create a feature
+ * with hdr=1 (0xbad00005). So every frame is encoded to a display-referred
+ * proxy first and the composite applies only the model's *delta*, scaled back
+ * by the same divisor the encode used:
+ *
+ *     den    = white + peak(linear)        (1.0 for SDR)
+ *     proxy  = srgb_encode(linear / den)
+ *     linear' = linear + den * (answer - proxy)
+ *
+ * This is NeuralScreen's pair, which is why HDR keeps its highlights: the
+ * divisor is per-pixel and derived from the anchor, so the proxy's highlights
+ * are compressed rather than clipped, and the delta is re-expanded by the
+ * anchor's own magnitude on the way out. No inverse tone mapping happens
+ * anywhere, and the output transfer is the input transfer.
+ *
+ * Dolby Vision:
+ *   P7 / P8    the decoded base layer is PQ BT.2020 YCbCr. We decode it to RGB
+ *              and run normally. The RPU reshape curves are not applied, and
+ *              the DoVi tag is dropped -- the frame that leaves this filter is
+ *              plain full-range PQ RGB, exactly as vsr and truehdr leave it.
+ *              Consequence for P7 FEL: the enhancement layer can no longer be
+ *              combined, because libplacebo's FEL merge expects a base layer
+ *              still in the DoVi domain, at the EL's resolution. The output
+ *              frame is therefore marked dovi-less and EL-less on purpose, so
+ *              el_pair discards the EL instead of stamping a DoVi tag onto
+ *              values that are no longer in that domain. Use `dovi=skip` for
+ *              a file where FEL detail matters more than NR.
+ *   P5         ICtCp (IPT), not YCbCr. There is no way to tell it apart from a
+ *              frame's pl_dovi_metadata: P5's RPU carries a full set of
+ *              matrices too, and libplacebo's mapping drops the two header
+ *              fields (vdr_rpu_profile, bl_video_full_range_flag) that
+ *              ffmpeg's own profile guess uses. So the decision is left to
+ *              the player, which does know the profile (mpv exposes
+ *              `current-tracks/video/dolby-vision-profile`); ai.conf keeps
+ *              profile 5 out of the chain entirely (its `-p5` profiles set no
+ *              vf at all, because ICtCp is not YCbCr at any stage). Getting it
+ *              wrong is not silent: P5 run as PQ YCbCr looks obviously wrong.
+ */
+
